# Cloudflare Workers static-asset headers. GitHub Pages ignores underscore-prefixed files, so
# this is inert on the current host and takes effect only once traffic moves to the Worker.
#
# No Content-Security-Policy here on purpose. The site loads GA4, Supabase and OCR.space, and
# every page carries inline <script>, so a CSP has to be built from a real inventory of those
# origins and shipped in Report-Only first. Adding a guessed one would break the calculator.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), payment=(), interest-cohort=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin

# Hashed/versioned nothing yet, so HTML must always revalidate while static assets may cache.
/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/sw.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/css/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

/js/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
